.obsidian/
__pycache__/
.venv/
*.pyc

# Toolkit-managed caches. _meta/.cache/ is written by the MCP framework itself:
# fts.db (an SQLite full-text index over every document) and siblings/ (cached
# sibling-corpus indexes for cross-corpus citation resolution). Neither is an
# input to anything — both rebuild on demand — and committing a binary SQLite
# file that changes on every ingest is exactly the kind of repository bloat that
# is painful to undo later.
_meta/.cache/

# Semantic-search artifact (vectors.i8.npy, chunks.jsonl, meta.json). Built on a GPU machine and never
# committed or baked. Today it is read only by the hybrid leg of `src/eval_questions.py --report`; this
# corpus's corpus.yml configures no semantic module, so the served tools do not use it. If the corpus is
# deployed with semantic search, it would be mounted read-only as oregon-budget and
# executive-regulatory-frameworks do. It must be ignored: a populated directory would otherwise add
# `?? _meta/embeddings/` to `git status --porcelain`, which is half of the FTS cache key.
# The --check gate never reads it.
_meta/embeddings/

# corpus-detect-changes writes this to the repo root on every run.
changed-sources.tsv

# GitHub Pages build output, if this corpus publishes a site.
site/

# Secret-shaped files. Nothing here should ever produce one, which is precisely
# why these are worth listing: a public civic-data repo gets no second chance
# once a credential is pushed, and the cost of the safety net is three lines.
*.env
.env
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json

.DS_Store

# The semantic-search artifact (vectors.i8.npy, chunks.jsonl, meta.json). Built on a GPU machine
# and bind-mounted read-only at /repo/_meta/embeddings by platform-deploy; never committed and
# never baked. It must be ignored: populating the mount would otherwise add `?? _meta/embeddings/`
# to `git status --porcelain`, which is half of the FTS cache key, so the index stamped at image
# build would be judged stale and rebuilt on the first request (same rule as oregon-kpm).
_meta/embeddings/
